cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use touchstone-mcp in academic, applied, or compliance work,
  please cite it using the metadata below. The Touchstone Standard
  and the clarethium-touchstone reference implementation are
  separately citeable artifacts with their own canonical references.
title: "touchstone-mcp: Model Context Protocol server for Touchstone"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lucic
    given-names: Lovro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9976-6933"
    website: "https://blog.clarethium.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Clarethium/touchstone"
url: "https://github.com/Clarethium/touchstone/tree/main/touchstone-mcp"
abstract: >-
  touchstone-mcp is the Model Context Protocol server that exposes
  the Touchstone calibrated Verifier and the raw measurement
  orchestrator to any MCP-compatible AI client (Claude Desktop,
  Claude Code, Cursor, custom). The server is a thin distribution
  wrapper around the clarethium-touchstone reference implementation;
  measurement semantics, calibration coefficients, and the eleven
  Section 5 measurement layers are defined in the Touchstone
  Standard and implemented in the clarethium-touchstone library.
  touchstone-mcp's contribution is reach: bringing the same
  hallucination-detection substrate to environments where the
  Python API is not directly callable.
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - hallucination-detection
  - fabrication-detection
  - structural-verification
  - touchstone
  - clarethium
  - claude-desktop
  - cursor
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-24"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "clarethium-touchstone: reference implementation of the Touchstone Standard"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lucic
        given-names: Lovro
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9976-6933"
    url: "https://pypi.org/project/clarethium-touchstone/"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Clarethium/touchstone"
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      The reference implementation that touchstone-mcp wraps. Imports
      Verifier, measure, and assess_derivation_regime from the public
      surface; defines the eleven Section 5 measurement layers and
      their calibration coefficients.
  - type: standard
    title: "Touchstone Standard 1.0 (draft)"
    version: "1.0.0-draft.15"
    url: "https://github.com/Clarethium/touchstone/blob/main/STANDARDS/touchstone-1.0.md"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    abstract: >-
      Draft specification for verification methodology whose scoring
      functions do not invoke an AI model on the output being
      measured. The MCP tools (verify, measure,
      assess_derivation_regime, list_modes) expose the Standard's
      Section 5 measurement layers via JSON-RPC.
